  ($q$RW-023$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Central Ideas and Details$q$, 2, $q$Contrary to the assumption that deep-sea environments are biologically barren, expeditions to hydrothermal vents have found dense communities of tube worms, crabs, and bacteria thriving without sunlight, sustained instead by chemical energy from the vents themselves.

