  ($q$RW-024$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Command of Evidence (Textual)$q$, 2, $q$A teacher argues that incorporating short daily writing exercises improves students' essay scores more than occasional long assignments do.

Which finding would most directly support the teacher's argument?$q$, $q$["Classes that wrote for 10 minutes daily improved average essay scores by 15%, while classes assigned one long essay per month showed no significant change.", "Writing is considered an important skill across many careers.", "Some students report disliking daily writing exercises.", "The school recently adopted a new writing curriculum."]$q$::jsonb, $q$Classes that wrote for 10 minutes daily improved average essay scores by 15%, while classes assigned one long essay per month showed no significant change.$q$, $q$The claim compares two specific approaches to writing practice; only choice A directly measures and compares outcomes for both groups.$q$, $q${"Writing is considered an important skill across many careers.": "A general claim about writing's value, unrelated to comparing daily vs. occasional practice.", "Some students report disliking daily writing exercises.": "A preference detail that doesn't address essay-score outcomes.", "The school recently adopted a new writing curriculum.": "An unrelated administrative fact that doesn't compare the two specific practice methods."}$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$published$q$),
  ($q$RW-025$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Inferences$q$, 3, $q$The company's founder has declined every interview request for over a decade, yet the firm's annual shareholder letter — written personally each year — reveals detailed opinions on everything from monetary policy to competitor strategy.

Which choice is the most logical inference based on the text?$q$, $q$["The founder avoids public appearances but is still willing to communicate views in writing.", "The founder has no opinions on monetary policy.", "The company has stopped publishing its shareholder letters.", "The founder is unaware of competitors' strategies."]$q$::jsonb, $q$The founder avoids public appearances but is still willing to communicate views in writing.$q$, $q$Declining interviews while personally writing detailed, opinionated letters each year implies a preference for written over spoken public communication, not a general aversion to sharing views.$q$, $q${"The founder has no opinions on monetary policy.": "Contradicts the passage, which says the letters reveal detailed opinions on monetary policy.", "The company has stopped publishing its shareholder letters.": "Contradicts the passage's statement that the letter is written 'each year.'", "The founder is unaware of competitors' strategies.": "Contradicts the passage's mention of opinions on 'competitor strategy.'"}$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$published$q$),
  ($q$RW-026$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Central Ideas and Details$q$, 3, $q$Octopuses solve mazes, open jars, and even appear to play, all despite having a nervous system organized radically differently from that of vertebrates — most of their neurons reside in their arms rather than in a central brain. Researchers increasingly view this decentralized intelligence not as a lesser version of vertebrate cognition but as an entirely distinct evolutionary solution to complex problem-solving.

Which choice best states the main idea of the text?$q$, $q$["Octopus intelligence, though structured differently from vertebrate intelligence, represents its own sophisticated evolutionary approach to problem-solving.", "Octopuses are considered less intelligent than most vertebrate species.", "All of an octopus's neurons are located in its central brain.", "Mazes are the only reliable way to test octopus intelligence."]$q$::jsonb, $q$Octopus intelligence, though structured differently from vertebrate intelligence, represents its own sophisticated evolutionary approach to problem-solving.$q$, $q$The passage explicitly reframes octopus cognition as 'an entirely distinct evolutionary solution,' not an inferior one — matching choice A and contradicting choice B and C.$q$, $q${"Octopuses are considered less intelligent than most vertebrate species.": "Reverses the passage's explicit reframing of octopus cognition as 'not... a lesser version' of vertebrate intelligence.", "All of an octopus's neurons are located in its central brain.": "Directly contradicts the passage's statement that most neurons reside in the arms, not a central brain.", "Mazes are the only reliable way to test octopus intelligence.": "Mistakes one example (maze-solving) for the only valid measure, an overstatement the passage never makes."}$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$published$q$),
  ($q$RW-027$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Command of Evidence (Quantitative)$q$, 2, $q$A public health official argues that a new vaccination campaign significantly reduced flu-related hospitalizations. Hospitalizations fell from 1,200 cases the prior flu season to 430 cases the season following the campaign, even as the region's population grew slightly.

