  ($q$RW-033$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Information and Ideas$q$, $q$Command of Evidence (Quantitative)$q$, 2, $q$An agricultural scientist argues that drip irrigation conserves significantly more water than traditional flood irrigation without reducing crop yield. Fields using drip irrigation used 35% less water per acre while yielding within 2% of the output from flood-irrigated fields.

